WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.121
The takeaway is that multi-class robust
classification has a large and now-measurable

00:00:05.201 --> 00:00:09.833
gap between what current defenses achieve and what
is theoretically possible,

00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:12.770
a gap that is far worse than in the binary case.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:18.399
The paper's conflict-hypergraph framework computes
the optimal 0-1 loss as a linear program,

00:00:18.479 --> 00:00:25.558
and its efficient truncated bounds pin that optimum
down tightly using only edges in the practical low-budget regime.

00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:31.494
This gives practitioners a fast diagnostic tool to
see how much robustness is still on the table,

00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:37.980
and it points future research toward closing the
gap rather than endlessly iterating attacks and defenses.
